---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="What Happens If You Skip Licensing — LicensingMadeSimple" description="Unlicensed activity can mean fines, a cease-and-desist, and unenforceable contracts. Confirm the required desk before you operate.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>What Happens If You Skip It</h1>
      <p>The consequences of operating without a required license.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container article" style="max-width: 720px;">
      <h2>Fines</h2>
      <p>Most jurisdictions can fine a business that operates without a required license. Some statutes treat each day as a separate violation. This site does not quote fine amounts — read the statute or the agency’s enforcement page for the jurisdiction you are in.</p>

      <h2>Forced shutdown</h2>
      <p>Agencies can issue a cease-and-desist that stops the activity until the license is in place. State financial regulators actively look for unlicensed collectors, lenders, money transmitters, and mortgage companies.</p>

      <h2>Contract problems</h2>
      <p>Contracts signed while unlicensed may be unenforceable. A contractor without a required license may not be able to collect in court. The other party can raise the missing license as a defense.</p>

      <h2>Personal liability</h2>
      <p>Operating without a required license can put personal assets at risk if something goes wrong. That is a legal question for counsel, not a filing-path question.</p>

      <h2>Find the required desk</h2>
      <p>Most licensing gaps are fixable once you know which agency takes the application. Use the <a href="/directory">directory</a> or the <a href="/#wizard">roadmap wizard</a>. If you want the filing prepared and submitted, <a href="https://cornerstonelicensing.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cornerstone Licensing</a> does that work.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .article h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 32px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .article h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .article p { font-size: 0.93rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 14px; }
</style>
